{"availability":"available","full":"nvpro-samples/vk_slang_editor","name":"vk_slang_editor","description":"A shader-driven livecoding tool using Vulkan and the Slang shading language.","category":"Developer tools","language":"C++","stars":60,"forks":2,"created":"2025-08-09T11:23:30Z","updated":"2026-10-06T10:41:30Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://shader-slang.org/slang-playground/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:35.545Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:35.545Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:35.545Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T16:43:35.545Z","stars":60,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A shader-driven livecoding tool using Vulkan and the Slang shading language. Download it here!","Vkslangeditor lets you write Slang shaders, compile them, and quickly see and interact with the result. Notably, it lets you write multi-pass pipelines in a single file, add arbitrary shader parameters, load meshes and textures; and much more -- while Slang's language features can make writing complex or large shaders easier.","This editor was initially created for the SIGGRAPH 2025 Introduction to Slang interactive lab. You can download the lab slides covering topics from basics to generics here, and the full lab materials (including SlangPy files) here!"],"features":["Supports compute, vertex, fragment, hull, domain, and geometry shaders","vkslangeditor automatically recognizes shader parameters named iTime, iFrame, iResolution, iMouse, iView, iProj, texFrame, and more, and will automatically write to them, converting to the data type used in the shader…","Pipelines and resources are defined inside shader code. If you need more offscreen buffers, for instance, adding another RWTexture2D to your global variables will create one!","Defining multiple entrypoints in a shader automatically combines them into passes and runs them every frame. This makes creating complex shader pipelines fast; for instance, see Examples > Siggraph2025 > Solutions > 2 -…","All unrecognized parameters will appear in the Shader Parameters GUI, so you can have as many sliders as you want to control your shader in real-time"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nvpro-samples/vk_slang_editor/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"2d80e16845f374caa6f16f52e10a32104fe9d190737fb8c49a6661bd4be06e9f","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:35.663Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:35.663Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A shader-driven livecoding tool using Vulkan and the Slang shading language. Download it here!","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nvpro-samples/vk_slang_editor/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"2d80e16845f374caa6f16f52e10a32104fe9d190737fb8c49a6661bd4be06e9f","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nvpro-samples/vk_slang_editor/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:35.663Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-06T10:41:30Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nvpro-samples/vk_slang_editor/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:35.664Z","hash":"2d80e16845f374caa6f16f52e10a32104fe9d190737fb8c49a6661bd4be06e9f","originalBytes":18798,"storedBytes":18798,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["slang","editor","shader","language","code","reflection","server","info","like","shaders","parameters","result","which","pipelines","uses","find","other","using","automatically","entrypoints","inside","might","type","cursor","doc","each","features","get","instance","module","move","pipeline","protocol","resources","run","see","slangd","spir-v","vulkan","write","buffers","ctrl","diagnostics","different","down","function","how","left","pane","pass","program","rendering","right","sets","shader.","shift","some","apps","check","data","delete","desc","descriptor","diagnostics.writeref","download","enter","here","layout","line","main","mode","much","ne